WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.133
Safety, part two.

2
00:00:02.433 --> 00:00:08.333
Seven more terms: moderation, leakage, explainability, documentation, and regulation.

3
00:00:09.533 --> 00:00:16.733
Content moderation classifies inputs and outputs for toxicity, violence, self-harm, and similar categories.

4
00:00:17.033 --> 00:00:22.533
You can use a provider's moderation endpoint, or a dedicated classifier like Llama Guard.

5
00:00:22.833 --> 00:00:24.800
Put them at the edges of your system.

6
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:35.667
Data leakage is your system revealing what it should not: system prompts, other users' context, training data, or retrieved but unauthorized documents.

7
00:00:35.967 --> 00:00:40.033
The rule: access control belongs in retrieval, not in the prompt.

8
00:00:41.233 --> 00:00:44.700
XAI is explainability for classical machine learning.

9
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:48.733
SHAP attributes a prediction to its features, using game theory.

10
00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:52.200
LIME fits a local surrogate model around the prediction.

11
00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.700
Expect this vocabulary wherever models make regulated decisions.

12
00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:01.233
Model cards are standardized model documentation.

13
00:01:01.533 --> 00:01:06.100
They state the intended use, the training data, the evals, and the limitations.

14
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:11.367
You read them on Hugging Face, and enterprises increasingly require you to write them.

15
00:01:12.567 --> 00:01:14.300
This is the governance triad.

16
00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:22.800
The EU AI Act is the binding, risk-tiered law, with general purpose AI obligations live from 2025.

17
00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:27.133
NIST AI RMF is a voluntary US risk framework.

18
00:01:27.433 --> 00:01:31.457
And ISO 42001 is the certifiable management standard.

19
00:01:31.457 --> 00:01:36.467
Know which is law, which is framework, and which is certification.

20
00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:43.543
Prompt leaking is when crafted queries extract your system prompt, tools, or configuration.

21
00:01:43.543 --> 00:01:47.933
The mistake is putting secrets, keys, or access rules in the prompt.

22
00:01:48.233 --> 00:01:52.733
The working assumption is that your prompt will leak, so keep all of that server-side.

23
00:01:53.933 --> 00:01:58.200
GDPR is the EU privacy law that AI systems inherit.

24
00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:05.700
It brings lawful basis for processing, data residency, and the awkward right to erasure question for trained models.

25
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.433
That is why enterprise deals specify regions and PII pipelines.

26
00:02:11.633 --> 00:02:12.396
Let's recap.

27
00:02:12.396 --> 00:02:15.000
Moderate inputs and outputs at the edges.

28
00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:18.767
Put access control in retrieval, and assume prompts will leak.

29
00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:23.233
SHAP and LIME explain predictions, and model cards document models.

30
00:02:23.533 --> 00:02:26.333
Know which is law, framework, or certification.

31
00:02:26.633 --> 00:02:30.767
And remember that GDPR shapes regions and PII handling.
